{
  "requirement": "A parse result MUST retain the source snapshot it describes. Cached parsing\nMUST NOT be paired with bytes from a different source snapshot.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.sources.provider_results.parse_snapshot`**\n1. A parse result retains the source snapshot it describes. The bytes in `ParsedSource.source` must be the bytes the outline was built from, and they must not change if the resource changes later.\n2. Cached parsing is never paired with bytes from a different snapshot. Consumers of a cached parse must use the cached snapshot's bytes and must not refetch or substitute other bytes.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- **Retention, default provider path.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/sources.rs#fn[defaults_use_provider_primitives_and_keep_one_parse_snapshot]` parses once from a `Memory` provider.\n  - It asserts that the parse used exactly one read (`reads == 1`) and that `parsed.source` starts with \"version 0\".\n  - It then reads a newer version and asserts that `parsed.source` still holds \"version 0\". It also asserts that the outline's `node_lines` contain \"version 0\", so the outline matches the retained bytes.\n  - The final event log shows no extra reads during parsing.\n- **Retention, local provider.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/sources.rs#fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` covers the sync and async parse paths.\n  - The two parse paths give equal bytes.\n  - After the file on disk is rewritten, a fresh `parse_sync` returns \"changed\". The earlier `retained` result still returns \"hit\\n\", and its outline still renders \"hit\".\n  - Failure cases for out-of-scope and outside-root resources return errors, so no stale or foreign snapshot is produced.\n- **Retention with language handling.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/sources.rs#fn[list_read_only_provider_supports_selected_language_parse_and_structural_search]` asserts `parsed.source.text() == provider.text`. It also asserts that the outline resolves against that same text, for both an explicit language and an extension-derived language.\n- **Cached parsing never paired with other bytes.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[cached_selected_source_reads_record_exact_delivered_contents_and_errors_add_no_input]` uses `CachedProvider`.\n  - `CachedProvider` overrides `parse` with a fixed snapshot built by `parse_snapshot`, and its `read` returns an error (\"must not refetch\").\n  - The graph's current source is set to a different value (\"different current source\").\n  - The test asserts that the recorded dependency fingerprint is exactly \"fn observed() { call(); }\", the cached snapshot's selected content. A refetch or a pairing with the graph's bytes would therefore fail the test.\n\n**Gaps**\nNo gaps found. The tests cover both clauses: retention across later changes, and cached parsing not being paired with different bytes. The assertions enforce the expected outcomes. All of these tests carry `{test}` references to the subject, so there are no marking gaps. There are no acknowledgments to assess.",
